NEGATIVE N01 zero-engines | selected engine list [] | reject before launch/write; never produce a success-looking empty report.
NEGATIVE N02 zero-rounds | rounds 0 | reject settings before launch/write.
NEGATIVE N03 zero-runs | engine chromium with runs [] and rounds 1 | reject before final write/read acceptance.
NEGATIVE N04 empty-intervals | run frames 0, intervalsMs [] | reject as no measured frame; no undefined percentile or null substitution.
NEGATIVE N05 missing-run | rounds 2, one engine has only three of the four P01 runs | reject incomplete round; do not calculate summary from one-sided data.
NEGATIVE N06 duplicate-run | repeat (engine chromium, round 1, baseline) | reject even if values are equal.
NEGATIVE N07 wrong-order | swap P01 chromium run[1] and run[2] | reject noncanonical alternating round/variant order; no silent reorder.
NEGATIVE N08 duplicate-engine | two engine records named chromium | reject even if browser versions differ.
NEGATIVE N09 bad-index | first run index 1 or a gap after index 0 | reject; never infer missing position.
NEGATIVE N10 missing-field | omit P01 run[0].navFilter while keeping cardFilter null or empty | reject missing required measurement; absent, null, and empty text are distinct.
NEGATIVE N11 wrong-units | declare frame intervals in seconds but use P01 millisecond values | reject mismatched unit/dimension, not silently rescale.
NEGATIVE N12 wrong-derived-value | P01 chromium run[3].over25Ms = 1 or p99Ms = 26 | reject inconsistent derived fields.
NEGATIVE N13 nonfinite | NaN, +Infinity, or -Infinity in any number cell | reject before write; never coerce to null or a string.
NEGATIVE N14 lone-surrogate | browserVersion contains unpaired UTF-16 high surrogate U+D800 | reject before write; never replace with U+FFFD.
NEGATIVE N15 unsupported-version | any version other than the explicitly accepted future version | reject; no silent fallback.
NEGATIVE N16 truncated-document | remove the final complete run or the final structural terminator from an otherwise valid encoded P01 document | reject, never accept partial success. Exact mutated bytes are pending the grammar.
NEGATIVE N17 resource-ceiling | one run/interval/text item exceeds a declared bound or total bytes/rows exceed its declared bound by one | reject before unbounded allocation. Numeric ceilings and exact byte examples are NOT FROZEN until P23 sizing/format choice; P04 is the admission floor.
NEGATIVE N18 incomplete-write | process stops after a temporary file is partly written | no final .measure path is published and no old .json path is overwritten.
NEGATIVE N19 nonpositive-interval | a captured frame delta is +0, -0, or negative | reject the measurement with a clear error before publication; do not silently filter the observation and report a plausible but incomplete count.

